  "behavior": [
    "IndexedMapNode repr(C) retains actual MapNode/ListValueNode/ListNode prefix at offset zero plus a native i32 index. Key1 aliases inherited Value/ChangeValue; Index is a mutable stored int, with no positivity validation.",
    "IndexedDataMapNode repr(C) retains existing DataMapNode/ListValueNode/ListNode prefix and its established value-before-key construction and key-before-value destruction. The added signed index has no destructor.",
    "Both native callback deleters release only their concrete node through the existing node_release guard, preserve successor nodes, and retain original pointer/allocator identity.",
    "One generic IndexedNodeAllocation wrapper delegates NativeNodeOwner for both new public owner aliases. No new ownership-release or member-unwind algorithm is duplicated.",
    "The only modification to DataMapNode is construct_parts visibility from private to pub(crate), enabling reuse of allocation-before-value-before-key construction factories. This is not a new public API.",
    "Inherited value/link access, pointer identity, mutable signed index including extremes, borrowed copy failures and Rust Drop-panic cleanup pass Miri. Rust panic cleanup checks are safety extensions, not native throwing-noexcept-destructor equivalence."
  ],
